{
  "_comment": [
    "Closed-class paradigms that OpenRussian ships without inflection data.",
    "These are the highest-frequency words in the language, so the gap is small in",
    "lemma count and huge in token count. Hand-authored; Russian closed-class",
    "morphology is finite and stable, so this file should rarely need edits.",
    "",
    "Slot naming matches OpenRussian so the renderer is shared:",
    "  pronouns    -> nom / gen / dat / acc / inst / prep",
    "  possessives -> decl_{m,f,n,pl}_{nom,gen,dat,acc,inst,prep}",
    "  verbs       -> presfut_{sg1,sg2,sg3,pl1,pl2,pl3}",
    "attach_to merges forms into an existing lemma instead of creating a new one.",
    "н-prefixed variants (него, ним) are the forms used after a preposition."
  ],

